*.jl.*.cov
*.jl.cov
*.jl.mem
*.rej
.DS_Store
.benchmarkci
Manifest.toml
# The code-health gate pins every version it depends on, and a committed Manifest is
# what makes that pin total. It is the only Manifest this repository tracks. ADR 0077.
!code_health/Manifest.toml
benchmark/*.json
coverage
docs/build/
# The docs build writes these four paths from `examples/**/*.jl`, `user_guide/*.jl`,
# `docs/capability_catalogue.jl` and `docs/generate_type_hierarchy.jl` on every run, and no
# workflow commits them back, so a committed copy is stale from the next docs change on. ADR 0151.
docs/src/examples/
docs/src/user_guide/
docs/src/capability_catalogue.md
docs/src/api/*_TypeHierarchy.md
env
node_modules
*NOTRACK*
*.CondaPkg/*
/docs/.CondaPkg/*
/test/.CondaPkg/*
/docs/node_modules/*
/docs/package-lock.json
.venv/
/graphify-out/
*ipynb
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# The Refresh Artifact is staged here by a failing check and uploaded by CI. It is never
# committed; the contributor puts the downloaded file at its committed path instead.
code_health/_refresh/
code_health/_triage/
code_health/_sweep/
